From 593ee48a3d2ae1a3f7669b28874bffc666ffeb9a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Raiju contributors <raiju@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 21:21:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: Bun.spawnSocket to run a program with its stdin and
 stdout on a Socket: a Unix socketpair end handed to the existing socket
 table, so data, write, backpressure and close work as they do for connect,
 with env, cwd and the usual SocketHandler (SIGTERM to the child when its
 parent dies, on Linux)

Tov had no way to start a process, so a program couldn't talk to a child process that speaks
newline-delimited JSON over its stdin and stdout, a common way to run tool servers. Bun.spawnSocket
runs the command with a socketpair as its stdin and stdout and returns the Socket for the
parent end. A program that can't start closes the socket at once, with the reason on stderr.
There is no exit status and stderr is inherited.

Tests: tests/run/native_spawn.tov runs a shell loop with an env var and a cwd, writes two
lines, checks the echoed output and the close event, and checks that a missing executable
closes its socket.
